          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "gabar — \"to boast (gabar-se); to praise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "O meu colega gaba-se sempre do carro novo. My colleague is forever boasting about his new car."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mostly reflexive, with the pronoun after the verb: gabar-se de — to boast about. Without -se, gabar alguém is to praise someone, a less common use."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "gabar comes from Occitan gabar \"to boast\" (EtymDB), which EtymDB traces to Old Norse gabb, a word usually glossed \"mockery\"."
            }
          ]
        },
